<article class="env-corollary" id="0F1E">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F1E">Corollary <span data-tag="0F1E">7.3.4.12</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a compact Hausdorff space. The global sections functor $\Gamma : \Shv (X) \rightarrow \SSet $ preserves filtered colimits. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Applying Theorem <a href="/tag/5B30" data-tag="5B30">7.3.4.9</a>, we can replace $\Shv (X)$ by $\Shv _{\calK }(X)$. Now observe that the full subcategory $\Shv _{\calK }(X) \subseteq \calP ( \Nerve (\calK (X))^{op})$ is stable under filtered colimits. We thereby reduce to proving that the evaluation functor $\calP ( \Nerve (\calK (X))^{op} ) \rightarrow \SSet $ commutes with filtered colimits, which follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/4396" data-tag="4396">5.1.2.2</a>. Alternatively, one can apply Corollary <a href="/tag/7C6D" data-tag="7C6D">7.3.4.10</a> and Remark <a href="/tag/81C4" data-tag="81C4">7.3.1.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>